      "hier_label_mismatch": "error",
      "label_dangling": "warning",
      "pin_not_connected": "warning",
      "pin_not_driven": "warning"
    },
    "_comment": "WIP severities. label_dangling, pin_not_connected and pin_not_driven are warnings because block interfaces are declared before the blocks that drive them exist - an empty sheet's hierarchical labels are legitimately unconnected, and a signal whose source block is not yet built genuinely has no driver. hier_label_mismatch stays an ERROR: a name or direction mismatch across a sheet boundary is always a real defect regardless of build state, and it is the check that proves the interface is self-consistent. Restore the three warnings to error once every block is populated. Tracked in docs/supervisor.md section 9."
  },
